1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,500
Meera: Arjun... close your eyes for a second.

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:05,060
Arjun: Okay. They're closed.

3
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:06,765
Meera: Now tell me...

4
00:00:06,765 --> 00:00:07,980
Meera: which side is red?

5
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:10,179
Arjun: Hmm... I can't.

6
00:00:10,179 --> 00:00:13,520
Arjun: Without my eyes, it's just... plastic.

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,920
Meera: One in twelve boys sees colour differently.

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,059
Meera: And some kids can't see colour at all.

9
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:20,804
Meera: The world's favourite puzzle...

10
00:00:20,804 --> 00:00:22,380
Meera: was only ever made for eyes.

11
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:24,614
Arjun: So what if the colours...

12
00:00:24,614 --> 00:00:25,440
Arjun: could be felt?

13
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,085
Meera: That's the LVC Dream Cube.

14
00:00:28,085 --> 00:00:30,627
Meera: Every colour gets its own texture.

15
00:00:30,627 --> 00:00:31,824
Meera: White is smooth.

16
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:35,040
Meera: Green has a raised frame. Orange... ridges.

17
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,460
Arjun: Wait, these are rings. So this is... red?

18
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,096
Meera: Red. Blue is dots.

19
00:00:41,096 --> 00:00:42,480
Meera: And yellow is...

20
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:45,180
Arjun: The big dome! I found it without looking!

21
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:50,223
Meera: Now a child who mixes up red and green never has to guess again.

22
00:00:50,223 --> 00:00:53,804
Meera: And blind and low-vision kids can solve it by touch...

23
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:55,660
Meera: right next to their friends.

24
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,180
Arjun: And for the rest of us?

25
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,558
Meera: Lights off. Phone down.

26
00:00:59,558 --> 00:01:03,620
Meera: Just you, the cube and your fingertips... before sleep.

27
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:05,920
Arjun: A puzzle... in the dark.

28
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:08,325
Meera: Right now it's a prototype.

29
00:01:08,325 --> 00:01:12,159
Meera: 3D-printed chips, glued onto an ordinary cube. It works...

30
00:01:12,159 --> 00:01:13,680
Meera: but it isn't ready yet.

31
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:15,660
Arjun: So that's where backers come in.

32
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:23,020
Meera: Yes. We'll test it with the kids it's meant for, make durable moulded chips, and add braille and audio instructions.

33
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,580
Arjun: And schools and NGOs get it for under ten dollars a cube.

34
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:29,159
Meera: Twenty-four ninety-nine for you...

35
00:01:29,159 --> 00:01:31,540
Meera: and every cube helps put one in a classroom.

36
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,340
Arjun: And the design files?

37
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,520
Meera: Free. Open source. For everyone.

38
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,494
Arjun: So one small change...

39
00:01:38,494 --> 00:01:41,840
Arjun: and a toy made for eyes becomes a toy made for everyone.

40
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:46,420
Meera: LVC Dream Cube. See it. Feel it. Solve it.

41
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,220
Arjun: Back us on Kickstarter.
